WEBVTT

00:01:07.548 --> 00:01:07.848
Thank you, Tom.

00:01:08.124 --> 00:01:08.344
Where?

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:11.260
On that ledge, sir, resting on a bit of the Tribune.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:12.960
Our most practical paper, Tenny.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:13.960
I'd rather like it, sir.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.280
Remind me to renew my subscription.

00:01:15.516 --> 00:01:16.876
It won't be necessary to resolve.

00:01:17.148 --> 00:01:20.868
And why not? Because a check for your subscription is already in the post.

00:01:21.884 --> 00:01:23.584
Ah, Kenny, you think of everything, don't you?

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:24.568
I hear you.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:25.360
tritons

00:01:26.556 --> 00:01:28.276
then think of some way to rescue my package.

00:01:29.116 --> 00:01:29.996
That's a...

00:01:30.028 --> 00:01:31.208
As they say in the books.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:32.680
You have me, sir.

00:01:34.572 --> 00:01:36.392
is one of my American cousins in the crowd.

00:01:36.656 --> 00:01:37.336
What's your name?

00:01:37.644 --> 00:01:39.104
Drummond, Captain, do you see Drummond?

00:01:39.244 --> 00:01:41.804
I ain't got no cousins for that name, but I'm an American, all right.

00:01:41.824 --> 00:01:43.804
Fine, then may I bottle a piece of your chewing gum?

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:44.704
CURANCE!

00:01:46.188 --> 00:01:47.288
Thank you. Don't mention it.

00:01:51.628 --> 00:01:52.448
All right, sir.

00:01:52.844 --> 00:01:53.484
Quite all right, Denny.

00:01:54.476 --> 00:01:55.656
Now, sir, may I borrow your stick?

00:01:56.108 --> 00:01:56.448
Thank you.

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:05.830
An excellent idea, though.

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:06.790
Colossal, Sennig.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:09.480
One night almost says stupendous, though.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:19.530
Yes, sir.

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:20.530
I've got it, sir.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:23.580
Now, thank you, sir.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:24.200
So, what idea?

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:27.030
My friend, I'm going to become a chewing-gun theme.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.060
Keeps the teeth nice and white.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:29.580
See?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:43.900
interesting. Here. Thank you. Don't mention it. You want any? Thank you. Bad, eh? I'd rather like it so. Say, mister, what's in that package?

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:45.790
Wedding rings.

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:51.940
Now that we have them, Tony, suppose we make a final check.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:52.580
Very well, sir.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.200
To begin with, I have the rings.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.580
No, sir, I have the rings.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:56.840
You have the rings.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:57.640
In my pocket, sir.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:02:58.500
The marriage papers?

00:02:58.680 --> 00:02:59.640
In your pocket, sir.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.710
Authorization for your wedding in Switzerland.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:03.070
Railway tickets?

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:08.040
Cars 7, London to Paris Express, leaving Victoria Station tonight.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:13.760
Plus, four kids are to be placed in Miss Phyllis' compartment at 9.50pm.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:14.930
Hotel accommodations?

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:16.950
Paris tomorrow morning at 9.50.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:17.270
So?

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:19.660
Two suites.

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.410
The following day in Geneva?

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:23.620
One suite.

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:26.850
Ah, Tony, getting married is great fun, isn't it?

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.190
In Switzerland, sir?

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.500
Anywhere, Tony, anywhere!

00:03:30.092 --> 00:03:31.252
popular belief, son.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.140
Tell me you're a pessimist.

00:03:33.548 --> 00:03:34.968
I've been very happy, sir.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:41.440
Captain Drummond.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:42.000
Yes, Johnny.

00:03:42.508 --> 00:03:43.968
When one is through with it,

00:03:44.396 --> 00:03:45.516
What does one do with it?

00:03:46.668 --> 00:03:46.988
seat.

00:03:47.372 --> 00:03:48.972
When one is done with it, what does one do with it?

00:03:49.012 --> 00:03:49.752
It was not a riddle.

00:03:50.668 --> 00:03:51.228
Well, then what is it?

00:03:51.328 --> 00:03:55.128
It's an academic inquiry as to how one disposes of one's chewing gum.

00:03:55.308 --> 00:03:56.468
Now I see him.

00:03:56.844 --> 00:03:58.184
Yeah, that does require force.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:03.380
Don't trouble, sir.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:04.620
And why not?

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:05.680
I've swallowed it, sir.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:10.730
Well, Kenny, that's one way.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.490
Hardly the right way, do you think, sir?

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:13.470
Time will tell.

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:15.170
Well, speaking of time, sir.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:19.070
At 4.30, I'm to call for Colonel Nielsen at Scotland Yard.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:28.440
Good afternoon, Captain Drummond.

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:29.570
On time to the dock.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.240
The telephone will be delayed a few moments.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:31.820
I'll wait.

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:33.740
And this clamoring telephone from Rockingham Lodge,

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:34.480
shall I get her for you?

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:35.420
Yes, will you please?

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:36.660
You may use the phone in there.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:37.270
Thank you.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:39.960
Rockingham Lodge, please.

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:42.900
Hello?

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:44.790
Oh, hello, dear.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:46.410
Got the rings?

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:47.360
Don't lose them.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:49.670
Now, in the first place, you called me...

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:50.910
To tell you that Gwen...

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:52.150
Asked you to tell me...

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.070
That Algie would meet you at Colonel Nielsen's office

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:55.010
and you could all come out...

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:55.290
Together.

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:57.130
All right, darling.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:57.630
See you soon.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:03.990
No, we'll see you in just a moment.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:07.920
Sumi Okanda.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:09.310
Hugh Drummond.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:10.970
Well, seven years haven't changed you.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:12.570
Nor you, my dear friend.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:14.570
And the English is more perfect than ever.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.730
Due largely to our most present scholastic association.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:20.310
Ah, that's the talk of a diplomat.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.240
That is kind.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:21.780
Are you?

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:22.990
Am I?

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.080
A diplomat.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:26.290
I see you have not forgotten.

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:26.950
What?

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:28.820
To ask questions.

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:30.630
Good-bye, Colonel.

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:31.420
Good-bye.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:32.160
Not at all, sir.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:33.380
I'll get hold of the Foreign Office immediately.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:34.000
Very good, sir.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:35.510
Mr. Kahn, though, Colonel Ilton.

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:36.150
How do you do, sir?

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:37.710
Just a few minutes.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:38.730
Do you step in, Mr. Kahn?

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:40.330
You'll forgive me?

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:40.810
Of course.

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:41.130
Go ahead.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.380
I trust my beat will not upset your plans.

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:52.960
Well, plans are made to be upset, aren't they?

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:53.700
That is so.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.360
That is why I am here.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.630
To try and upset some plans.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:58.340
Sit down.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:05:58.820
Thank you.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:04.050
Do you know who and what I am?

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:04.630
Of course.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:06.800
We understand each other then.

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:15.250
Between us, representing in a separate way the interest of two friendly nations, there need to be no evasion.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:16.260
That is so?

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:17.070
Quite.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.000
Then I'll tell you something of great importance.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:21.120
Concerning?

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:22.520
Sir John Huckston.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:24.060
How do you know?

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.780
How I know is not of importance.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:29.980
Sir John Huckston has invented a...

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:38.420
Super explosive, an ultra-powerful combination of destructive elements for use in airplane bombs.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:44.190
He's leaving today for France to confer with munition chemist of your great ally.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:45.110
That is so?

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:46.220
Go on.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:51.690
An attempt will be made to steal the portion of experimental supply he's taking with him.

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:52.370
How do you know this?

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:53.320
Please.

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:59.650
A single airplane carrying a hundred small bombs loaded with...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.520
This devastating force could destroy any capital in the world.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.440
Has it ever occurred to you, my dear Mr. Kanda,

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.940
an espionage might be a rather dangerous pastime?

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:12.500
Now is not time for accusation or decrimination.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:17.160
My country and your country, too, are in great danger

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:21.100
if Sir John's discovery falls into unfriendly hunt.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:23.940
Suppose I were to tell you there's no such thing as this explosion.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.060
We agreed not to wait.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:29.370
Please, I'm a friend. I wish to cooperate.

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:29.970
Tell me.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:36.090
everything oh that i know i'll see sir john at once yes of course that will be proper goodbye i

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:51.210
get sir john haxton on the wire at once captain drop is waiting send him in ready cuddle bye you

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:55.120
i'm ready to run along without me you mean you're not coming to the station with us i didn't say

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:59.020
that i said you'll have to run along without me and then you will be there later yes later

